# Staging Environment Secrets Template
#
# This file documents the required secrets for the staging environment.
# Add these secrets to GitHub: Settings → Environments → staging → Environment secrets
#
# DO NOT commit actual secret values to this file!

# ============================================================================
# Database Configuration
# ============================================================================

# PostgreSQL connection string for staging database
# Format: postgresql://username:password@host:port/database
# Example: postgresql://push_user:staging_pass@staging-db.example.com:5432/push_platform_staging
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/database

# ============================================================================
# Firebase Configuration
# ============================================================================

# Firebase project ID for staging (development mode)
# This is used for FCM push notifications in development
# Get this from Firebase Console → Project Settings → General
# Example: my-push-platform-staging
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-firebase-project-id

# ============================================================================
# API Security
# ============================================================================

# Comma-separated list of valid API keys for staging
# Generate secure random keys (minimum 32 characters)
# Example: staging-key-abc123,staging-key-def456
API_KEYS=staging-key-1,staging-key-2

# ============================================================================
# Deployment URLs (Optional)
# ============================================================================

# Staging API URL for health checks and deployment tracking
# Example: https://api-staging.example.com
# If not set, health checks will be skipped
API_URL=https://api-staging.example.com

# Staging Worker URL for deployment tracking
# Example: https://worker-staging.example.com
# Used for deployment status updates
WORKER_URL=https://worker-staging.example.com

# ============================================================================
# Platform-Specific Secrets (Optional)
# ============================================================================

# Only add these if you're using the specific platform for deployment

# Railway
# Get from Railway Dashboard → Settings → Tokens
# RAILWAY_TOKEN=your-railway-token

# Google Cloud Run
# Service account JSON key (download from GCP Console)
# GCP_SA_KEY={"type":"service_account","project_id":"..."}
# GCP_PROJECT_ID=your-gcp-project-id

# AWS ECS/Fargate
# Get from AWS IAM → Users → Security credentials
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-aws-access-key
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-aws-secret-key

# Generic Docker Host (SSH)
# SSH credentials for deployment
# SERVER_HOST=staging.example.com
# SERVER_USER=deploy
# SSH_PRIVATE_KEY=-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----...

# ============================================================================
# Instructions
# ============================================================================
#
# 1. Copy this template to use as reference
# 2. Generate actual secret values (never use example values in production)
# 3. Add secrets to GitHub:
#    - Go to repository Settings
#    - Click Environments
#    - Select "staging"
#    - Click "Add secret"
#    - Enter secret name and value
#    - Click "Add secret"
# 4. Verify secrets are set before running deployment workflows
#
# For detailed instructions, see: .github/DEPLOYMENT.md
